        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-14T00:25:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "also, one more concern about this: could this result in time between INT_AP_L pulses shorter than 100 us, in turn causing a lost pulse?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 408,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 408,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "b6773cd5f9c499ca062fceee0d827802b32bf5f1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "815b34fc_72657ab4",
        "filename": "chip/g/sps.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 408,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-14T00:39:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it can make INT_AP_L pulse shorter, which is intended.\n\nAP transaction is roughly\n1. tpm_sync()   /* recognize INT_AP_L assertion or waiting for it. */\n2. spi_claim()  /* assert SPI_CS */\n3. read status, read|write command|data ...\n4. spi_release() /* deassert SPI_CS */\n\nSo, I expect if AP asserted SPI_CS then, it means it recognized INT_AP_L assertion, and Cr50 doesn\u0027t need to keep it asserted.",
      "parentUuid": "2f342bbd_0f7b3832",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 408,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 408,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "b6773cd5f9c499ca062fceee0d827802b32bf5f1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8bfc67f_7933df20",
        "filename": "chip/g/sps.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 408,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-14T04:29:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Realized that I misread your comment: it possibly could shorten the duration of INT_AP_L DEASSERTION. Actually, it might shorten the duration of ASSERTION, not DEASSERTION. Deassertion duration should be observed by ap_start_ack_completion() line 276~280",
      "parentUuid": "815b34fc_72657ab4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 408,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 408,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "b6773cd5f9c499ca062fceee0d827802b32bf5f1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "884065cd_69acd8ac",
        "filename": "chip/g/sps.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 408,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-14T20:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "right, this one is about shortening \"ready\" assertion, if AP already starts sending the next packet. if it does, whatever happened on AP side - it either recognized the pulse already, or decided to move forward w/o getting the \"ready\" signal from cr50 - it doesn\u0027t need to have \"ready\" asserted anymore.\n\nand with spi this logic can be applied to CS assertion, which can only happen before AP decides to send the next packet (even if AP somehow decided to send CS wake-up pulse while we are still holding the \"ready\" pulse).",
      "parentUuid": "a8bfc67f_7933df20",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 408,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 408,
        "endChar": 28
      },
